      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 758857798873088
    m_Localized: The cafe sells coffee and various soft drinks, also some salty and
      sweet snacks.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 761345482518528
    m_Localized: "Suupohja's employment area includes Isojoki, Karijoki, Kauhajoki,
      Kristiinankaupunki, Kurikka and Teuva. Emplayment services provided by Vuoksi.\n\nPrivate
      customer service: 040 5478 375 (mon\u2013fri 9\u201315)\n tyollisyysalue@vuoksi.fi\n\nEmplayers
      and companies: 040 5652 085\n\nAuthority line: 040 5643 553 (only calls, no
      text messages)"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 763615834107904
    m_Localized: "Vuoksi offers advice for immigrants, employers and businesses in
      regards to, integration, learning the finnish language, international recruitment
      and more.\nhttps://vuoksi.fi/tyohon/kansainvalisyyspalvelut/\n\nMaahanmuuttokoordinaattori
      Agnes Szeman\n 040 641 6374\n agnes.szeman@vuoksi.fi"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 764662195515392
    m_Localized: "Kauhajoki's clothes bank is a free recycling point, where one can
      get childrens', teens' and adults' clothing, practice equipment and home textiles.
      Donations are to be recieved in good condition and clean. The clothes bank
      operates from Vuoksi's B-building's Tekomo.\n\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/people/Momssit-Kauhajoki/61577383570980/\n
      Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/momssit_kauhajoki"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 768067513184256
    m_Localized: 'Emplayment area

      info point'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 768366663528448
    m_Localized: Health centre
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1087139186569216
    m_Localized: People and culture
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1089984531099648
    m_Localized: 'Finnish culture values equality, honesty and privacy. People can
      first seem untalkative, but are often friendly and helpful.


      Suupohja''s
      local culture can be seen at events, exhibits and soceietal functions. Libraries,
      galleries and culture events offer a low barrier to entry way to get to know
      the finnish way of life.

      More information about culture: https://finland.fi


      Cafes
      and community spaces are great places to meet new people.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1094841702903808
    m_Localized: Health and wellbeing
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1095092094464000
    m_Localized: 'Health services in Finland are high quality and broad. Public healthcare
      acts through heath centers, and in busy situations the ER helps. Additionally
      you can find provate doctors, dentists and pharmacies.


      Kela supports
      you with healthcare expences.

      More information: https://www.kela.fi


      Wellbeing
      isn''t just about health. It''s also about exersice, rest and social relationships.
      Suupohja has gyms, public swimming pools and outdoor recreation areas.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1100461327872000
    m_Localized: Work and entrepreneurship
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1100991487897600
    m_Localized: 'Work is an important part of integration. In Finland searching
      for work often happens through TE-services, recruitung sites and through connections.
      The CV and job applications are central tools.


      Entrepreneurship is
      also a good option and help for it can be found through business services.

      More
      information: https://tyomarkkinatori.fi | https://www.yrityssuomi.fi


      Suupohja
      has multiple opportunities from different fields. Local businesses value know-how
      and motivation.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1108773423378432
    m_Localized: Moving to Suupohja
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1108914687537152
    m_Localized: 'A new start in Suupohja starts with the basics of everyday life:
      housing, registration and finding local services. Douring your  move to Finland,
      you must register your residency and address, and you must aquire a finnish
      social security number. Digital and population data services agency (DVV) and
      Finnish immigration service (Migri) help with these steps.

      More information:
      https://dvv.fi | https://migri.fi


      Life in Suupohja is peaceful, close
      to nature, and services are easily accessible. This application helps you find
      rental apartments, postal services, banks, important places of business and
      more. Douring the beginning stages of a move, it is recommended to familiarize
      oneself with local libraries and help desks, where one may get free advice.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
